       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe, and I want you to confirm it first.\n\n- **Order as written:** metformin 1700 mg PO TID, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day. Individual doses are usually no more than 1,000 mg. This order is about twice the daily maximum.\n- **Risk:** Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- 1,700 mg total per day, such as 850 mg BID\n- 850 mg PO TID (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,000 mg PO BID or TID with meals\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg TID, please confirm that explicitly. I'd also suggest adding a note with the clinical rationale."
      }
